{
  "_about": "Every MCP tool Cecelia registers, and what KIND of thing it does — the one list. Each server's `_tool` registrar refuses a tool missing here, and turns its kind into MCP ToolAnnotations (tool_kinds.py). Read by mcp/tests/test_server.py (registered == listed), frontend/src/lib/claudeTools.test.ts and utils/guideMap.test.ts (the user-facing tool list, the ✦ pages), and api/test/suite/kiwi_turn.jl (Kiwi reads only `read` tools). `observer` = cecelia-observer; `autonomous` = cecelia-autonomous's OWN tools — it also registers the observer's gating and figure toolsets.",
  "kinds": {
    "read": "reads project or app state; changes nothing",
    "add": "adds something new beside the user's own (a population, board, figure, chain, notebook, note, project data); only when asked",
    "edit": "changes or removes something that already exists — only what Claude made, or a view setting saved like a hand change",
    "point": "draws a short-lived mark on the user's screen; nothing is saved",
    "drive": "moves the user's screen (a frame, a page); nothing is saved",
    "run": "starts work (tasks, chains) — the autonomous server only",
    "report": "drafts a bug report on this machine for the user to send; never posts it",
    "plumbing": "session bookkeeping (pairing, the observer loop); not a capability"
  },
